# GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2: React Router RSC (React Server Components) mode
# CSRF bypass. Both apps use client-side routing only (BrowserRouter/
# HashRouter, no server actions, no RSC) — this mode isn't reachable in
# either codebase. Fixed in react-router@8.3.0, which requires React
# >=19.2.7; upgrading is a separate, larger decision already deliberately
# deferred (both apps are pinned to React 18.2.0 — see ROADMAP.md's
# Phase 8/10 notes, pre-deletion, or git log). Revisit when that upgrade
# actually happens, not by silently ignoring this forever.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2

# CVE-2026-14257: brace-expansion ReDoS. This tree has two live major
# lines of brace-expansion with incompatible APIs: 1.1.16 via the older
# minimatch@3 (ESLint's own @eslint/config-array), and 5.x via
# minimatch@10 (typescript-eslint) — the latter is patched via a
# pnpm-workspace.yaml scoped override, but no fix was ever released
# within the 1.x line itself (only in 5.x), so minimatch@3's copy can't
# be patched without forcing an API-incompatible major bump onto code
# that doesn't expect it — confirmed this breaks ESLint entirely by
# testing it directly. Dev/lint-time only, parsing this repo's own
# trusted glob patterns, never attacker-controlled input — not shipped
# in either app's client bundle.
CVE-2026-14257
